docs(oracle): note PYTH_VERIFICATION_FEE is an intentional cost trade-off

The fixed 1-wei verification fee paid from the contract balance keeps the
price-update path cheap; if Pyth raises its on-chain verification_fee above
this, pushes revert until the constant is bumped (redeploy) — accepted.

